<title>JAPAN: Speculative shares fall on loss-cut sales.</title>
<headline>Speculative shares fall on loss-cut sales.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Incentive-backed, speculative shares fell in the Friday morning session, due to loss-cut sales by investors, brokers said.</p>
<p>At the lunch break, Sumitomo Seika, which was second on the most heavily traded list, was down 19 yen at 914 yen, after hitting a low of 888 yen, Its trade volume as 3.263 million shares. Nichiboshin, the third on the list, ended the session up two yen at 542 yen but only after falling as low as 501 yen. Its trade volume was 2.744 million shares.</p>
<p>Daido Steel Sheet was down 10 yen at 1,050 after reaching a low of 995 yen.</p>
